PROPOSED, NOT APPLIED. Owner decision INF-02 (docs/debt-consolidation/27-PRODUCTION-INFRASTRUCTURE-READINESS.md section 6).

The locked Composer dependencies (Symfony 8 components) require PHP >= 8.4.1
(vendor/composer/platform_check.php), but the runtime stage uses PHP 8.3, so an
image built from this Dockerfile stops every request with Composer platform
error. This predates Debt Consolidation. The test suite runs on PHP 8.5, so
the patch moves the runtime to 8.5; 8.4 would also satisfy the dependencies.
Build it and run the smoke tests on a staging host before production.

Check:  git apply --check docs/debt-consolidation/release/dockerfile-php-runtime.patch

--- a/Dockerfile
+++ b/Dockerfile
@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@
 ##
 ## 3) Runtime image: php-fpm + nginx + supervisor
 ##
-FROM php:8.3-fpm-alpine AS app
+FROM php:8.5-fpm-alpine AS app
 
 RUN apk add --no-cache \
         nginx \
